<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pratap Singha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1603">1603</a>–<a href="/years/1641">1641</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Susenghphaa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pratap Singha, or Susenghphaa, was king of the Ahom kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> from 1603 to 1641. He created the offices of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borbarua">Borbarua</a> and the Borphukan, reorganised the paik labour system through his official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/momai-tamuli-borbarua">Momai Tamuli Borbarua</a>, and fought a long war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamrup">Kamrup</a> that ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-asurar-ali">Treaty of Asurar Ali</a> in 1639. His reign is regarded as a high point of Ahom state-building.</p></div>
